From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: use ETH-lane JCPLL tuning for USXGMII on the PON PCS

The XR1710G wires the wan port (gdm2) to the PON PCS. When that lane
runs USXGMII at 10G it needs the ETH-lane JCPLL TCLVAR (0x5): keeping
the PON value (0x3) makes the 10G link train degraded and the peer
drops the link about 1 s after every AN completion, while the same
cable and peer hold 10G on the ETH PCS port (lan2).

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -764,8 +764,14 @@
 	 * its own the value is not what makes the ETH lane work, see
 	 * an7581_pcs_jcpll_recal().
 	 */
+	/* The XR1710G wires the wan port (gdm2) to the PON PCS. When that
+	 * lane runs USXGMII at 10G it needs the ETH-lane JCPLL tuning:
+	 * keeping the PON value (0x3) makes the 10G link train degraded
+	 * and the peer drops it ~1 s after every AN completion.
+	 */
 	regmap_field_write(pcs_ana_fields[AN7581_PCS_JCPLL_VCO_TCLVAR],
-			   priv->data->port_type == AIROHA_PCS_ETH ? 0x5 : 0x3);
+			   (priv->data->port_type == AIROHA_PCS_ETH ||
+			    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII) ? 0x5 : 0x3);
 
 	/* Setup PCW */
 	regmap_update_bits(pcs_pma, AIROHA_PCS_PMA_PXP_JCPLL_SDM_PCW,
